WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.635
Students photocopied

00:00:01.447 --> 00:00:02.449
this Unix book

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.380
for twenty years

00:00:03.918 --> 00:00:05.109
John Lions wrote

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.934
a commentary on

00:00:05.746 --> 00:00:06.795
the Unix Version

00:00:06.607 --> 00:00:07.726
6 source code

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.696
and by 1977 his

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:10.875
notes were circulating

00:00:10.687 --> 00:00:12.078
among schools and

00:00:11.984 --> 00:00:13.316
research institutions

00:00:13.128 --> 00:00:14.625
with Unix licenses

00:00:15.166 --> 00:00:16.203
Even Bell Labs

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.041
wanted copies

00:00:17.088 --> 00:00:18.338
and eventually took

00:00:18.149 --> 00:00:19.340
over distribution

00:00:19.479 --> 00:00:20.446
But for roughly

00:00:20.258 --> 00:00:21.601
twenty years before

00:00:21.413 --> 00:00:22.427
the official edition

00:00:22.239 --> 00:00:22.899
appeared

00:00:23.147 --> 00:00:24.373
students studied from

00:00:24.361 --> 00:00:26.094
unauthorized photocopies

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:27.443
The book helped

00:00:27.255 --> 00:00:28.174
a generation of

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:28.988
students learn to

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.132
build operating systems

00:00:29.944 --> 00:00:30.651
of their own

00:00:30.805 --> 00:00:31.665
and the official

00:00:31.477 --> 00:00:33.068
edition finally appeared

00:00:32.892 --> 00:00:34.413
in 1996

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:35.964
Full story on

00:00:35.775 --> 00:00:36.671
the dashboard
